    card title "Bigger and better"

A: How do you say bigger or better in Russian, when you compare two things?
    draw a_big a_big_n

A: Take two cities: Moscow, and Oslo.
    draw a_small a_small_n

B: Москва́ бо́льше, чем О́сло.
    draw g_open

A: Word for word: Moscow bigger than Oslo. Бо́льше is bigger, and there's no is, as in сего́дня хо́лодно.
    highlight g_open_w_2 effect underline color #8f887c

B: Чем is than, and in writing a comma goes before it.
    highlight g_open_w_3 effect underline color #8f887c

    erase pageA

A: Four compare words today, each paired with a word you know. Then a trick that makes many more.
    draw k1 k2 k3 k4

A: Бо́льше comes from lesson twelve's большо́й, big, with the stress moved to the front.
    draw row1

B: Small was ма́ленький, but smaller is short and new: ме́ньше.
    draw row2

A: Better is new too, just as it is in English: хорошо́, good, becomes лу́чше.
    draw row3

B: And пло́хо, bad, from lesson thirty-eight's мне пло́хо, becomes ху́же, worse.
    draw row4

    hide c1 c2 c3 c4

A: All four end in е, and Russian compare words mostly do.
    draw cc1 cc2 cc3 cc4 parallel true

    hide boardB2

B: Москва́ бо́льше, чем Ло́ндон: Moscow is bigger than London.
    draw gt1 s1

A: Ло́ндон бо́льше, чем О́сло: a he this time, and бо́льше stays the same.
    draw gt2 s2

B: And for me, ле́то лу́чше, чем зима́: summer is better than winter.
    draw gt3 s3

A: Unlike большо́й, with its four endings, a compare word has just one form.
    highlight s2 effect underline color #8f887c part бо́льше

    hide boardC

    quiz "Росси́я is a she-word. Which word fills the gap? Росси́я ___, чем Норве́гия." store chk reveal.text "Росси́я бо́льше, чем Норве́гия" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a
        right: Бо́льше: a compare word has one form for he, she and it.
        wrong: Больша́я just says big. Which word compares?
        + бо́льше
        * больша́я

    erase question_1_stamp

    show boardC

B: After чем, the second thing takes the same form as the first: Москва́ and Ло́ндон, ле́то and зима́, all plain.
    highlight s3 effect underline color #8f887c part зима́

    erase boardC

A: Бо́льше also means more: мне бо́льше нра́вится ко́фе, чем чай. I like coffee more than tea.
    draw d_coffee d_tea d_more

    erase d_coffee d_tea d_more

B: Now the trick, for many other words.
    draw d_sun

B: Drop the last о and add е́е, with the stress on it.
    draw d_warm

B: Тепло́, warm, becomes тепле́е, warmer.
    draw d_warm_e

B: Сего́дня тепле́е, чем вчера́: today it's warmer than yesterday.
    draw d_today

    erase d_sun d_warm d_warm_e d_today

A: Now I'm visiting Masha in Moscow, and we compare it with London.
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name parallel true

    dialogue talk speakers.a tom speakers.b masha turns [{"by":"a","text":"Москва́ бо́льше, чем Ло́ндон?","gloss":"Is Moscow bigger than London?"},{"by":"b","text":"Да, бо́льше.","gloss":"Yes, it's bigger."},{"by":"a","text":"А где лу́чше?","gloss":"And where is it better?"},{"by":"b","text":"Ле́том — в Москве́!","gloss":"In summer, in Moscow!"}] size 1.3

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw talk

    erase talk

    dialogue talk2 speakers.a tom speakers.b masha turns [{"by":"a","text":"А зимо́й?","gloss":"And in winter?"},{"by":"b","text":"Зимо́й тут ху́же. В Ло́ндоне тепле́е!","gloss":"In winter it's worse here. London is warmer!"}] size 1.3

    draw talk2

A: No чем there: when it's clear what you compare with, you can leave it out.
    highlight talk2_2_words effect underline color #8f887c part тепле́е

    erase talk2

    hide speakers

    quiz "Oslo is smaller than Moscow: О́сло ___, чем Москва́. Which word fills the gap?" reveal.text "О́сло ме́ньше, чем Москва́." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: Ме́ньше is smaller, the short new word for ма́ленький.
        wrong: Which one is smaller, not bigger or worse?
        * бо́льше
        + ме́ньше
        * ху́же

    erase question_2_stamp

    ask "For Tom, coffee is better than tea. Type the missing word: Ко́фе ___, чем чай." answer ["лучше"] reveal.text "Ко́фе лу́чше, чем чай." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЫЬЭЮЯ
        right: Лу́чше: хорошо́ becomes лу́чше, better.
        wrong: Start from хорошо́: better is a new word.

    erase question_3_stamp

    quiz "What does Зимо́й тут ху́же mean?" say_answer false reveal.text "Зимо́й тут ху́же." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Ху́же is worse, from пло́хо.
        wrong: Ху́же comes from пло́хо, bad.
        + In winter it's worse here.
        * In winter it's better here.
        * In winter it's colder here.

    erase question_4_stamp

    quiz "Moscow is bigger than Berlin: Москва́ бо́льше, ___ Берли́н. Which word fills the gap?" reveal.text "Москва́ бо́льше, чем Берли́н." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: Чем is than, with a comma before it.
        wrong: Which word means than?
        * и
        + чем
        * или

    erase question_5_stamp

    quiz "Today it's colder than yesterday: Сего́дня ___, чем вчера́. Which word fills the gap?" reveal.text "Сего́дня холодне́е, чем вчера́" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 400 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Холодне́е: хо́лодно drops its last о and adds е́е, like тепло́ and тепле́е.
        wrong: Do with хо́лодно what тепло́ did to make тепле́е.
        * хо́лодно
        + холодне́е
        * ху́же

    erase question_6_stamp

    show k1 k2 k3 k4 ar1 ar2 ar3 ar4 cc1 cc2 cc3 cc4

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

    draw k5 ar5 cc5 chem

A: So a compare word ends in е and never changes: бо́льше, ме́ньше, лу́чше, ху́же, and the тепле́е kind, with чем for than.
    highlight ccol effect underline color #8f887c

    hide recap

B: And to you: вы говори́те по-ру́сски лу́чше, чем вчера́, better than yesterday! Next time: done or doing. Пока́!
    icon end_up size 160 set twemoji x 500 y 500 or ["thumbs up","ok hand"] icon_look picture of "thumbs up"
    text end_say "Вы говори́те по-ру́сски" say "Вы говори́те по-ру́сски лу́чше, чем вчера́!" say_voice b x 500 y 340 font_size 52
    text end_say2 "лу́чше, чем вчера́!" say "Вы говори́те по-ру́сски лу́чше, чем вчера́!" say_voice b colors {"лу́чше":"#c27c0e"} x 500 y 260 font_size 52

